WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.841
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.111 --> 00:55.076
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
01:01.249 --> 01:02.250
Who?

4
01:02.834 --> 01:04.502
I don't know anyone by that name.

5
01:05.086 --> 01:05.962
"Keum Seo-hee."

6
01:08.756 --> 01:11.593
Don't you know what that name means to So-ran?

7
01:13.928 --> 01:15.180
Her husband,

8
01:16.973 --> 01:18.641
the man you met today,

9
01:18.725 --> 01:20.894
refused to turn in his comrades.

10
01:20.977 --> 01:23.313
That's why Sato killed his daughter.

11
01:26.316 --> 01:27.942
Right in front of So-ran's eyes.

12
01:32.780 --> 01:34.949
Even if our cause doesn't make sense to you,

13
01:36.701 --> 01:37.660
think about So-ran.

14
01:39.454 --> 01:41.789
Can't you understand her goal?

15
01:43.750 --> 01:45.418
I know you think it's crazy.

16
01:45.501 --> 01:47.295
But if one lost their beloved child overnight,

17
01:47.378 --> 01:49.631
anyone would have done the same.

18
01:53.718 --> 01:55.011
Please.

19
01:56.095 --> 01:57.889
Try to understand So-ran.

20
02:30.255 --> 02:32.632
Out of the way. Traitors are dealt with. Remember?

21
02:32.715 --> 02:33.883
We need to bring her back.

22
02:33.967 --> 02:34.884
Why would we do that?

23
02:34.968 --> 02:36.177
We need to tie up loose ends.

24
02:36.261 --> 02:38.429
She did her job as a spy properly.

25
02:38.513 --> 02:40.014
Why should we kill her?

26
02:40.098 --> 02:41.683
We're the ones who didn't trust her.

27
02:41.766 --> 02:43.685
She just said she's out.

28
02:44.602 --> 02:46.020
If she goes running her mouth--

29
02:46.104 --> 02:48.564
She has no intention of betraying us.

30
02:49.941 --> 02:52.277
She said she's scared of getting caught and killed.

31
02:52.360 --> 02:55.571
That means betraying us to save herself isn't even on her mind.

32
02:55.655 --> 02:56.990
She's terrified of dying

33
02:57.073 --> 02:58.491
if her cover is blown.

34
02:58.574 --> 03:02.704
But even in that situation, turning on us isn't an option for her.

35
03:02.787 --> 03:03.621
Don't you get it?

36
03:05.039 --> 03:07.959
She's the spy we sent to kill Sato.

37
03:08.042 --> 03:10.336
We shouldn't be trying to kill her right now.

38
03:10.878 --> 03:13.298
We should be trying to convince her to come back.

39
03:23.933 --> 03:25.310
Just this once.

40
03:27.770 --> 03:29.731
I won't try to persuade her again.

41
04:07.643 --> 04:08.853
Hideo.

42
04:08.936 --> 04:10.104
Hanako?

43
04:10.646 --> 04:11.481
Hanako.

44
04:11.564 --> 04:13.483
-Hanako. -Hideo.

45
04:13.566 --> 04:14.567
Hanako.

46
04:14.650 --> 04:16.736
Hideo must be tired. He needs some rest--

47
04:16.819 --> 04:17.904
Let go!

48
04:19.405 --> 04:20.406
Hideo.

49
04:20.490 --> 04:23.034
I wrote all the capital letters.

50
04:23.117 --> 04:24.369
Look.

51
04:24.452 --> 04:27.121
Hanako, I'm sorry.

52
04:27.205 --> 04:29.374
I'm a bit tired today. How about next time?

53
04:29.457 --> 04:30.750
Next time? When?

54
04:30.833 --> 04:32.919
You always come home late.

55
04:33.002 --> 04:36.172
Look. I memorized all the capital letters.

56
04:36.255 --> 04:37.090
Hanako.

57
04:37.673 --> 04:39.592
Maybe tomorrow. I promise I'll look.

58
04:39.675 --> 04:41.219
You're a liar!

59
04:42.303 --> 04:44.847
You always come late, and you always say, "Maybe tomorrow."

60
04:44.931 --> 04:47.141
You're not going to keep your promise!

61
04:47.225 --> 04:49.060
I need some space today, okay?

62
04:54.690 --> 04:56.192
I hate you!

63
05:09.664 --> 05:10.998
Don't worry about Hanako.

64
05:11.082 --> 05:12.458
I'll go check on her.

65
05:12.542 --> 05:13.626
Good night.

66
05:27.557 --> 05:29.058
You insolent Josenjing!

67
05:32.019 --> 05:32.854
Come in.

68
05:36.357 --> 05:37.191
Father.

69
05:40.153 --> 05:41.112
Well done.

70
05:41.863 --> 05:42.989
Sorry?

71
05:43.072 --> 05:43.990
What do you mean?

72
05:46.492 --> 05:47.994
Even if you're slapped,

73
05:48.077 --> 05:50.913
a true Japanese must show no emotion.

74
06:02.758 --> 06:04.427
Sit upright, Hideo.

75
06:06.304 --> 06:07.889
Japanese people don't sit like that.

76
06:10.933 --> 06:13.769
From now on, never let your thoughts or feelings

77
06:14.437 --> 06:15.771
show on your face.

78
06:16.814 --> 06:18.691
That's what makes you Japanese

79
06:18.774 --> 06:19.942
and my son.

80
06:20.526 --> 06:21.777
Do you understand, Hideo?

81
06:26.574 --> 06:27.408
Answer me.

82
06:28.159 --> 06:29.660
Yes, Father.

83
06:31.787 --> 06:34.332
Father.

84
06:35.625 --> 06:36.542
Well done.

85
06:39.045 --> 06:39.879
Thank you.

86
06:39.962 --> 06:43.049
You didn't think Fukuda would get much out of questioning him,

87
06:43.549 --> 06:44.675
did you?

88
06:45.927 --> 06:46.844
No.

89
06:46.928 --> 06:48.721
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee was called in

90
06:48.804 --> 06:50.640
and didn't return for seven hours.

91
06:51.390 --> 06:53.434
If it'd gone well, it wouldn't have taken that long.

92
06:55.728 --> 06:56.854
You have a point.

93
06:58.731 --> 06:59.774
Keum Seo-hee.

94
07:00.983 --> 07:01.817
Yes?

95
07:02.944 --> 07:04.654
Did you make sure she won't speak?

96
07:05.947 --> 07:08.658
If Yoo Philip writes an article, it'll be a problem.

97
07:09.700 --> 07:10.535
Okay.

98
07:12.787 --> 07:14.622
She's going to rely on you a lot.

99
07:15.665 --> 07:17.875
Even if she's dating an American reporter,

100
07:18.918 --> 07:21.504
she's one of the few women in the Government-General

101
07:21.587 --> 07:22.672
and a Joseon person at that.

102
07:23.673 --> 07:24.799
I don't really follow…

103
07:24.882 --> 07:27.301
I assume everything she sees, hears, and thinks

104
07:28.219 --> 07:29.929
is passed on to Mr. Yoo.

105
07:31.430 --> 07:33.307
Get her to rely on you

106
07:33.391 --> 07:34.725
and trust you.

107
07:37.687 --> 07:38.813
But keep this in mind.

108
07:40.022 --> 07:41.524
She needs to trust you,

109
07:42.275 --> 07:44.694
but you must never trust her.

110
07:46.529 --> 07:48.489
Joseon people are an untrustworthy bunch.

111
07:49.448 --> 07:50.491
And Joseon women

112
07:51.909 --> 07:53.494
are bound to betray us.

113
07:57.248 --> 07:58.833
That's exactly what your mother did.

114
08:01.335 --> 08:03.296
She promised to spend her life with me,

115
08:05.631 --> 08:06.674
only to leave me.

116
08:45.671 --> 08:47.423
I know you think it's crazy.

117
08:47.506 --> 08:49.467
But if one lost their beloved child overnight,

118
08:49.550 --> 08:52.053
anyone would have done the same.

119
08:54.847 --> 08:55.848
Anyone…

120
08:57.099 --> 08:58.434
Her damn mother

121
08:58.517 --> 09:01.812
dumped her own kid to sleep around with a Jap.

122
09:03.022 --> 09:03.856
-A Jap? -With a Jap…

123
09:03.939 --> 09:06.484
When my mom left me…

124
09:09.654 --> 09:11.614
I resented her a lot, naturally.

125
09:12.907 --> 09:16.869
But as time went on, I started telling myself…

126
09:18.704 --> 09:19.997
that my mom

127
09:20.998 --> 09:23.626
had just found someone she loved more,

128
09:24.377 --> 09:26.379
but that she still loved me too.

129
09:29.256 --> 09:30.132
So…

130
09:31.717 --> 09:34.845
I was just a little unlucky.

131
09:35.638 --> 09:37.348
I wasn't a pitiful kid.

132
09:38.099 --> 09:42.311
That's what I've believed all this time.

133
09:47.024 --> 09:48.567
But seeing you,

134
09:50.319 --> 09:54.323
I find myself a little jealous of Seo-hee.

135
10:01.122 --> 10:04.166
Because her mother is willing to risk her life

136
10:05.167 --> 10:06.877
for her daughter.

137
10:29.942 --> 10:30.943
Did you sleep well?

138
10:34.822 --> 10:36.657
Assassinating the inspector general.

139
10:37.408 --> 10:39.994
How long will you need? If you move quickly.

140
10:42.872 --> 10:43.706
A month.

141
10:47.418 --> 10:48.794
All right, one month.

142
10:50.087 --> 10:51.046
That's it.

143
10:52.548 --> 10:53.424
After one month,

144
10:53.966 --> 10:56.135
send me to America, no matter what.

145
10:58.554 --> 10:59.430
Okay.

146
10:59.972 --> 11:01.098
I promise.

147
11:02.433 --> 11:03.267
Thank you.

148
11:05.978 --> 11:07.438
Just one month. Don't forget.

149
11:20.117 --> 11:26.540
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

150
11:26.624 --> 11:27.625
JONGNO POLICE STATION

151
11:27.708 --> 11:29.168
EPISODE 6

152
11:36.133 --> 11:37.176
Zip it!

153
11:38.594 --> 11:40.012
Still alive?

154
11:40.095 --> 11:41.347
They're like cockroaches.

155
12:00.574 --> 12:02.576
I looked into the thing you asked about.

156
12:03.285 --> 12:05.788
I managed to get in touch with the Gugukdan.

157
12:05.871 --> 12:08.415
It turns out the Gugukdan was planning to kill Sato

158
12:08.916 --> 12:11.710
that very day we went to the American reporter's house.

159
12:12.336 --> 12:15.714
I'm not sure if the American reporter was part of the Gugukdan,

160
12:15.798 --> 12:17.258
but I did find out one thing.

161
12:17.925 --> 12:20.219
They've got a female sniper in their group.

162
12:21.595 --> 12:23.722
They say she's as good as Nam Ja-hyeon.

163
12:24.723 --> 12:26.642
But I don't know her name or any details.

164
12:35.860 --> 12:38.279
Did you know your fellow members were killed in Dongsung-dong?

165
13:23.616 --> 13:24.575
You're all set.

166
13:25.576 --> 13:26.619
Thank you.

167
13:33.125 --> 13:34.293
So, about that man.

168
13:35.210 --> 13:36.587
Seo-hee's father.

169
13:37.379 --> 13:40.090
I'll find a way.

170
13:41.550 --> 13:42.760
Find a way for what?

171
13:45.262 --> 13:48.265
He tried to assassinate the inspector general of the Government-General.

172
13:48.349 --> 13:49.433
We know how the trial will end.

173
13:50.768 --> 13:52.978
Even if he's lucky enough to avoid execution,

174
13:53.062 --> 13:55.814
how long can he hold out with those injuries?

175
13:55.898 --> 13:57.274
Even perfectly healthy men

176
13:57.358 --> 13:59.902
come out of that prison in body bags.

177
14:09.620 --> 14:11.038
We don't have time to waste.

178
14:11.121 --> 14:13.916
We have to act now to keep them from torturing him.

179
14:13.999 --> 14:15.209
I'll go talk to Sato.

180
14:15.292 --> 14:16.877
-Once I meet him-- -Once you do,

181
14:18.629 --> 14:19.797
what are you planning to do?

182
14:19.880 --> 14:22.800
I'll tell him I'm interested in the Kyeam-ri incident.

183
14:24.301 --> 14:26.679
I could ask to speak with one of the prisoners.

184
14:26.762 --> 14:30.265
Once that happens, even Sato will have to think twice before acting.

185
14:35.020 --> 14:37.106
What Sato wants to hide the most

186
14:37.189 --> 14:39.900
is the Kyeam-ri massacre being brought back into the spotlight.

187
14:43.737 --> 14:45.489
The mastermind of the Kyeam-ri massacre, Sato,

188
14:45.572 --> 14:46.824
no, Ishikawa,

189
14:47.658 --> 14:50.995
leveraged his in-laws' connections to become the inspector general.

190
14:51.078 --> 14:55.290
He even took his wife's family name, Sato, to claw his way up to the top.

191
14:55.374 --> 14:59.044
So, with the world's eyes on Japan right now because of Manchukuo,

192
14:59.128 --> 15:02.089
if Sato thinks I might publish the Kyeam-ri story--

193
15:02.172 --> 15:03.215
And then what?

194
15:08.637 --> 15:10.097
What difference will it make?

195
15:11.348 --> 15:14.018
If the foreign press picks it up with Manchukuo at stake,

196
15:14.101 --> 15:16.895
Sato might have to step down as inspector general.

197
15:16.979 --> 15:18.439
But even if that happens,

198
15:19.481 --> 15:21.233
is that what we're fighting for?

199
15:21.316 --> 15:22.484
Is that enough?

200
15:25.654 --> 15:28.449
If I kill Sato, I can die with no regrets.

201
15:28.532 --> 15:31.535
But remember, that's when your fight begins.

202
15:33.037 --> 15:34.872
You pledged to expose the truth

203
15:34.955 --> 15:37.291
about Japan's and Sato's atrocities under your name

204
15:37.374 --> 15:39.168
and make sure the whole world sees it.

205
15:39.251 --> 15:41.545
So until then, you have to maintain good terms

206
15:41.628 --> 15:44.298
with the Government-General as an American journalist.

207
15:48.719 --> 15:52.181
If Sato realizes he was one of the victims from the Kyeam-ri massacre,

208
15:52.264 --> 15:54.725
there's a chance he'll find out who I am.

209
15:56.477 --> 15:58.270
He'll probably keep quiet,

210
15:58.353 --> 15:59.563
but you never know.

211
16:03.859 --> 16:07.196
So leave that to fate and don't do anything.

212
16:07.279 --> 16:09.698
Even if he dies in prison,

213
16:10.324 --> 16:11.700
there's nothing we can do.

214
16:11.784 --> 16:14.453
But, So-ran, he's your husband.

215
16:14.536 --> 16:15.370
No.

216
16:18.332 --> 16:20.375
You are my husband.

217
16:44.483 --> 16:45.609
SATO HIDEO KEUM SEO-HEE

218
16:45.692 --> 16:47.277
Win Sato Hideo's heart.

219
16:48.320 --> 16:49.780
Get him on your side.

220
16:50.280 --> 16:52.783
The inspector general keeps people at arm's length.

221
16:52.866 --> 16:55.202
But Sato Hideo is one of the few people close to him.

222
16:55.786 --> 16:56.703
All right.

223
16:56.787 --> 16:57.955
But remember.

224
16:58.038 --> 17:00.374
Never let yourself have personal feelings.

225
17:01.250 --> 17:02.292
Don't worry.

226
17:03.043 --> 17:04.962
That's never going to happen.

227
17:07.673 --> 17:08.715
Hello…

228
17:32.990 --> 17:34.867
Get her to rely on you

229
17:34.950 --> 17:36.285
and trust you.

230
17:36.994 --> 17:38.120
But keep this in mind.

231
17:38.620 --> 17:40.205
She needs to trust you,

232
17:40.873 --> 17:43.750
but you must never trust her.

233
18:20.454 --> 18:21.663
There's nothing special.

234
18:38.889 --> 18:39.765
What is that?

235
18:55.405 --> 18:56.573
You're here?

236
19:03.747 --> 19:05.374
"The inspector general's secretary."

237
19:06.291 --> 19:08.001
"Yamada Hanako."

238
19:08.794 --> 19:10.796
"The niece of the Internal Affairs Bureau director."

239
19:11.463 --> 19:13.632
"She can't speak the Joseon language."

240
19:13.715 --> 19:15.717
"Sloppy with work."

241
19:16.551 --> 19:18.095
"A good kid at heart."

242
19:20.097 --> 19:22.099
"She seems to have a crush on Sato Hideo."

243
19:25.310 --> 19:27.437
Wait, why on earth?

244
19:32.442 --> 19:33.694
Hello.

245
19:35.153 --> 19:37.155
Ms. Yamada, the inspector general's secretary?

246
19:37.239 --> 19:38.407
Yes.

247
19:41.118 --> 19:42.995
Is Mr. Sato in?

248
19:43.870 --> 19:45.414
He hasn't come in yet.

249
19:45.998 --> 19:47.207
Not yet?

250
19:48.166 --> 19:49.126
When will he be in?

251
19:49.209 --> 19:51.712
Well, I'm not sure.

252
19:53.297 --> 19:55.215
Should I tell him you stopped by?

253
19:55.299 --> 19:56.258
No.

254
19:57.175 --> 19:58.385
Just give him this.

255
20:00.304 --> 20:02.848
We received a lot of cookies at the Inspector General's Office.

256
20:04.891 --> 20:07.561
Please give these to Mr. Sato.

257
20:08.145 --> 20:10.188
Sure. I'll make sure he gets them.

258
20:10.272 --> 20:11.898
Thank you.

259
20:33.503 --> 20:34.671
Just one.

260
20:52.147 --> 20:53.648
LADIES' ROOM

261
20:58.487 --> 21:00.614
He says he can't put up with this.

262
21:01.239 --> 21:02.199
NO ENTRY

263
21:02.282 --> 21:03.283
Go ahead.

264
21:24.137 --> 21:24.971
Translate it.

265
21:34.898 --> 21:37.109
The Joseon workers are being worked too hard,

266
21:37.192 --> 21:38.902
and they're falling ill one after another.

267
21:38.985 --> 21:41.279
He says pushing them too hard to meet the deadline

268
21:41.863 --> 21:43.448
will backfire on us.

269
21:43.532 --> 21:45.117
So he wants their working hours reduced

270
21:45.200 --> 21:48.245
and enough time for rest.

271
21:49.663 --> 21:52.207
How many hours a day are they working?

272
21:52.290 --> 21:55.127
Fourteen hours. It's been three months straight without a day off.

273
21:57.504 --> 21:59.256
Cut their hours by an hour every other day.

274
22:00.590 --> 22:01.425
But…

275
22:02.843 --> 22:05.095
if they miss the deadline,

276
22:05.178 --> 22:07.222
they'll be held accountable.

277
22:08.056 --> 22:08.890
Got it.

278
22:18.483 --> 22:19.317
Well, then.

279
22:20.444 --> 22:21.278
Let's go.

280
22:49.431 --> 22:50.891
Interpreter Sato.

281
22:50.974 --> 22:51.808
Yes, sir.

282
22:54.269 --> 22:56.354
Did you interpret that correctly today?

283
22:58.273 --> 22:59.649
What makes you think I didn't?

284
23:02.277 --> 23:03.445
All right, I trust you.

285
23:09.951 --> 23:12.787
Have the workers work an hour longer every day.

286
23:13.788 --> 23:14.623
Father.

287
23:14.706 --> 23:16.708
Why should we go easy on them?

288
23:17.959 --> 23:19.544
They must meet the deadline.

289
23:20.629 --> 23:21.755
That's an order,

290
23:22.255 --> 23:23.173
Interpreter Sato.

291
23:33.058 --> 23:35.477
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO

292
23:47.531 --> 23:48.907
You're here?

293
23:50.825 --> 23:53.161
I was doing some cleaning.

294
23:53.245 --> 23:55.038
You weren't coming, and I had nothing else to do.

295
23:55.121 --> 23:56.790
So I figured I might as well clean.

296
23:59.167 --> 24:01.419
By the way, where have you been?

297
24:02.170 --> 24:04.381
I was worried since you didn't come in without a word.

298
24:05.882 --> 24:07.050
Look at all this dust.

299
24:08.051 --> 24:09.553
If I don't wipe it down,

300
24:09.636 --> 24:12.305
we'll end up breathing all of it in.

301
24:21.273 --> 24:22.107
Ms. Keum.

302
24:23.817 --> 24:24.651
Yes?

303
24:27.070 --> 24:29.739
Yesterday was hard on you, wasn't it?

304
24:30.657 --> 24:31.491
Sorry?

305
24:32.075 --> 24:34.035
You won't be called in for anything like that again.

306
24:36.538 --> 24:38.873
It's okay. I wouldn't mind doing it again.

307
24:39.833 --> 24:40.667
What?

308
24:41.543 --> 24:44.129
When I got home and thought about it,

309
24:44.921 --> 24:46.464
I realized I was angry at him.

310
24:46.548 --> 24:48.383
I nearly died because of him too.

311
24:49.092 --> 24:50.093
I was startled,

312
24:50.176 --> 24:53.430
but that was because I faced the man who tried to kill me before.

313
24:53.513 --> 24:54.973
I'm okay now.

314
24:55.056 --> 24:56.057
Just a little tired.

315
24:57.559 --> 24:59.769
If I get called up for another interrogation,

316
24:59.853 --> 25:01.187
I want to do a better job.

317
25:03.231 --> 25:07.402
I didn't mention anything to Mr. Yoo, as you asked,

318
25:07.485 --> 25:08.737
so don't worry.

319
25:14.284 --> 25:15.827
Oh, one more thing.

320
25:15.910 --> 25:20.582
You haven't found that Jongno Pawnshop yet, have you?

321
25:22.459 --> 25:25.170
I'll help you find it.

322
25:25.253 --> 25:27.213
I know Jongno like the back of my hand.

323
25:27.297 --> 25:28.298
You can count on me.

324
25:28.882 --> 25:29.966
I'll help you.

325
25:33.345 --> 25:34.179
No thanks.

326
25:34.929 --> 25:35.889
What?

327
25:35.972 --> 25:37.974
I don't need your help.

328
25:38.850 --> 25:42.562
I can take care of my own business. Just give me the pawn ticket you stole.

329
25:43.355 --> 25:46.107
I've played along with your game long enough now.

330
25:46.191 --> 25:48.026
Now bring me my pawn ticket.

331
25:53.281 --> 25:54.115
Come in.

332
26:00.413 --> 26:01.289
Excuse me.

333
26:01.373 --> 26:05.752
The chief of police sent me to bring Ms. Keum Seo-hee to Jongno Police Station.

334
26:05.835 --> 26:08.505
It's for the interrogation of the same person from yesterday.

335
26:11.466 --> 26:12.717
Good for you.

336
26:12.801 --> 26:14.928
Have a nice time.

337
26:15.011 --> 26:17.263
You said you wanted to do better next time.

338
26:18.640 --> 26:19.974
Well, actually…

339
26:21.309 --> 26:23.937
he told me to bring you along as well, sir.

340
26:38.034 --> 26:38.952
Chief.

341
26:40.245 --> 26:43.289
I thought we'd agreed that the Foreign Affairs Division

342
26:43.373 --> 26:45.875
would no longer provide interpreters for interrogations.

343
26:46.459 --> 26:49.838
We tried another interpreter, but he kept asking for Keum Seo-hee.

344
26:50.547 --> 26:52.090
What else could I do?

345
26:53.967 --> 26:58.430
Did you two hit it off yesterday while I wasn't looking?

346
26:58.513 --> 27:00.390
That is completely inappropriate, Chief.

347
27:01.224 --> 27:02.308
Otherwise,

348
27:02.392 --> 27:05.353
why would he be asking for Keum Seo-hee?

349
27:05.437 --> 27:07.897
We already have an interpreter at the station.

350
27:07.981 --> 27:08.940
So why ask for her?

351
27:09.023 --> 27:12.360
You asked for Ms. Keum yourself yesterday as well,

352
27:13.445 --> 27:15.405
when there's an interpreter here.

353
27:15.488 --> 27:16.614
Didn't you?

354
27:18.032 --> 27:21.244
We'll just have to find out why he specifically requested

355
27:21.327 --> 27:22.912
interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee.

356
27:23.580 --> 27:24.622
Fair enough.

357
27:25.623 --> 27:29.627
The inspector general heard about this

358
27:30.128 --> 27:32.255
and ordered Interpreter Sato to sit in

359
27:32.338 --> 27:35.425
to ensure the interrogation goes smoothly.

360
27:35.508 --> 27:37.927
I'm truly touched

361
27:38.887 --> 27:41.264
by his thoughtfulness.

362
27:48.521 --> 27:49.606
My goodness.

363
27:49.689 --> 27:50.815
Tell me about it.

364
27:51.399 --> 27:53.860
Mr. Sato kindly joined me today.

365
27:53.943 --> 27:56.780
I think I'll be able to do a better job interpreting.

366
27:57.280 --> 27:59.365
Interpreter Sato Hideo

367
27:59.449 --> 28:03.328
speaks Japanese, English, and the Joseon language, so…

368
28:05.371 --> 28:06.498
I'm sorry.

369
28:07.165 --> 28:10.585
I accidentally used the Joseon language in front of you.

370
28:11.169 --> 28:13.004
I just said Interpreter Sato Hideo

371
28:13.087 --> 28:16.049
can speak Japanese, English, and the Joseon language.

372
28:16.132 --> 28:18.760
Of course. He's an interpreter, after all.

373
28:18.843 --> 28:20.845
Yes, that's right.

374
28:23.431 --> 28:26.726
Since Interpreter Sato Hideo speaks the Joseon language fluently,

375
28:26.810 --> 28:31.397
I'll need to be extra careful with my interpretation.

376
28:31.481 --> 28:34.192
He'll catch any mistakes right away.

377
28:36.653 --> 28:37.570
Let's begin.

378
28:38.279 --> 28:39.113
Yes, sir.

379
28:42.075 --> 28:44.494
No, I'll observe from the back.

380
28:54.212 --> 28:55.213
Your name?

381
28:55.964 --> 28:57.173
What's your name?

382
29:00.301 --> 29:02.345
Let me ask you again. What's your name?

383
29:02.428 --> 29:03.930
He's asking you again.

384
29:04.556 --> 29:05.557
What's your name?

385
29:07.600 --> 29:10.019
I granted your request, so shouldn't you cooperate?

386
29:10.103 --> 29:11.980
I brought your interpreter.

387
29:12.063 --> 29:14.482
-I'll ask you again. What's your name? -Answer him.

388
29:14.566 --> 29:16.734
What's your name?

389
29:18.111 --> 29:18.987
E…

390
29:21.573 --> 29:22.657
Go on.

391
29:25.618 --> 29:28.246
Tell me, what's your name?

392
29:30.206 --> 29:31.666
Eat…

393
29:34.502 --> 29:35.628
shit.

394
29:35.712 --> 29:37.088
You son of a bitch!

395
29:45.972 --> 29:47.223
Typical Josenjing.

396
29:47.307 --> 29:49.767
You just run that filthy mouth of yours.

397
29:50.852 --> 29:53.980
You lot are all the same, Josenjing.

398
29:55.982 --> 29:58.318
You can try to hide what's inside,

399
29:58.401 --> 30:00.612
but you stink in the end.

400
30:01.112 --> 30:04.449
It always gives you away, Josenjings.

401
30:08.036 --> 30:09.954
Chief, we brought her here.

402
30:11.039 --> 30:11.915
Oh yeah?

403
30:13.166 --> 30:14.876
-Go ahead. -Yes, sir.

404
30:30.642 --> 30:32.644
Na Byeong-sun, you have a visitor.

405
31:08.054 --> 31:08.930
Honey.

406
31:13.142 --> 31:13.977
Honey.

407
31:15.311 --> 31:16.479
Honey!

408
31:18.272 --> 31:19.732
Forgive us.

409
31:19.816 --> 31:22.568
Please forgive us!

410
31:23.277 --> 31:24.112
Honey.

411
31:24.904 --> 31:25.863
Honey.

412
31:26.489 --> 31:29.492
Please forgive us.

413
31:32.829 --> 31:34.747
Honey!

414
31:57.979 --> 31:58.813
Young-bok.

415
32:03.776 --> 32:04.944
Why are you up?

416
32:05.862 --> 32:07.238
You need to stay in bed.

417
32:08.906 --> 32:09.741
I'm fine.

418
32:09.824 --> 32:11.325
I'll go to my room now.

419
32:12.035 --> 32:13.244
No, don't worry.

420
32:13.327 --> 32:14.662
My dad has no idea.

421
32:17.749 --> 32:21.127
The floor must be uncomfortable. You can't sleep well on the floor.

422
32:27.467 --> 32:28.426
Fine.

423
32:29.802 --> 32:31.512
Have some pine-nut porridge before you go.

424
32:33.473 --> 32:34.432
No, thank you.

425
32:36.184 --> 32:37.393
I'll just take this.

426
32:38.519 --> 32:39.645
Well, then.

427
32:40.980 --> 32:42.106
Thank you.

428
32:48.154 --> 32:49.697
You silly fool.

429
32:50.782 --> 32:53.743
Do you think I couldn't sleep because I was on the floor?

430
32:58.414 --> 32:59.999
Oh my, the bandages.

431
33:18.351 --> 33:21.854
DON'T YOU DARE DIE

432
33:37.703 --> 33:38.538
Please, have some.

433
33:39.122 --> 33:39.956
Thanks.

434
33:49.298 --> 33:55.012
How is the pneumatic tube project coming along?

435
33:55.096 --> 33:57.223
We're in the final stretch.

436
33:58.307 --> 34:01.519
Thank you once again for your generous donation.

437
34:03.813 --> 34:07.275
It brings immense pride to my family.

438
34:07.817 --> 34:10.236
It was my lifelong regret that I couldn't contribute

439
34:10.319 --> 34:14.782
even a single brick when this building was being built.

440
34:18.161 --> 34:20.955
I'm sure you're here to see how the tube installation is going.

441
34:21.789 --> 34:23.749
You should have a look. It's on the first floor.

442
34:24.333 --> 34:26.252
Wait, Inspector General.

443
34:26.335 --> 34:27.170
Well…

444
34:30.506 --> 34:31.674
Here.

445
34:33.759 --> 34:35.720
This is my daughter.

446
34:44.645 --> 34:47.440
I was hoping I could have dinner at home tonight.

447
34:52.069 --> 34:53.112
Chief.

448
34:54.989 --> 34:58.534
May I try speaking with him in our language?

449
35:01.037 --> 35:03.039
We're both Joseon people,

450
35:03.122 --> 35:05.666
so I'll see if I can convince him to talk.

451
35:05.750 --> 35:10.004
What are you people plotting, speaking your language behind my back?

452
35:12.006 --> 35:12.965
That's right.

453
35:13.049 --> 35:16.260
Why don't you two Joseon people have an intimate conversation?

454
35:17.136 --> 35:18.679
Should I get you a room?

455
35:18.763 --> 35:20.014
Chief!

456
35:22.183 --> 35:23.809
There's no need to worry.

457
35:25.102 --> 35:27.188
Even if you don't trust me,

458
35:27.271 --> 35:30.483
Interpreter Sato here speaks the Joseon language,

459
35:30.566 --> 35:32.109
and he's keeping an eye on us.

460
35:34.528 --> 35:35.613
Fine, let's see what you can do.

461
35:39.533 --> 35:41.369
Thank you, sir.

462
35:50.753 --> 35:51.671
When you

463
35:52.588 --> 35:55.800
snuck into the house as a deliveryman,

464
35:56.300 --> 35:57.468
I was the live-in maid there.

465
35:58.344 --> 36:00.763
You pointed a gun at me that day.

466
36:02.515 --> 36:05.768
If you'd ever tried to kill my madam,

467
36:05.851 --> 36:08.020
I would've found a way to stop you.

468
36:08.104 --> 36:10.273
That is, if you'd tried to kill her.

469
36:13.985 --> 36:17.905
She's Chinese, so she doesn't speak the Joseon language very well.

470
36:19.532 --> 36:21.701
But she's really good to me.

471
36:22.618 --> 36:26.914
She gave me the pretty name Keum Seo-hee.

472
36:28.499 --> 36:29.792
I wonder

473
36:29.875 --> 36:33.337
how she came up with such a pretty name for me.

474
36:35.923 --> 36:38.050
Anyway, I'm completely on her side.

475
36:42.763 --> 36:43.639
Hey.

476
36:44.682 --> 36:45.850
You're dragging this out.

477
36:45.933 --> 36:47.184
What are you saying?

478
36:48.269 --> 36:49.395
I'm sorry.

479
36:50.021 --> 36:54.066
I was making small talk to get him to open up.

480
37:00.865 --> 37:03.492
Did you know your fellow members were killed in Dongsung-dong?

481
37:06.787 --> 37:08.622
Yesterday, in Dongsung-dong…

482
37:10.499 --> 37:12.084
Did he just say Dongsung-dong?

483
37:14.503 --> 37:15.713
He's finally talking.

484
37:16.464 --> 37:17.506
What is he saying?

485
37:18.132 --> 37:20.176
What happened to the people who got away?

486
37:21.635 --> 37:23.888
I heard they'd been shot.

487
37:26.015 --> 37:27.767
What's he saying?

488
37:29.685 --> 37:32.271
He's asking what happened to those who were wounded and escaped

489
37:32.355 --> 37:33.981
yesterday in Dongsung-dong.

490
37:36.025 --> 37:37.443
I'll try to get him

491
37:37.526 --> 37:39.570
to talk about something else.

492
37:40.529 --> 37:41.906
Fine.

493
37:43.407 --> 37:46.911
You want to know if your comrades who fled yesterday are safe, right?

494
37:50.206 --> 37:52.500
Of course. I understand how you feel.

495
37:52.583 --> 37:54.794
Whenever something dangerous happens,

496
37:54.877 --> 37:56.962
I immediately worry about my madam first.

497
37:57.546 --> 38:00.925
When she saw me off this morning,

498
38:01.008 --> 38:05.096
I just hoped she'd stay safe and live a long life.

499
38:19.068 --> 38:22.279
Chief, his accomplice gave us his name.

500
38:22.363 --> 38:24.740
Is that so?

501
38:24.824 --> 38:26.409
How did you get it out of him?

502
38:26.492 --> 38:28.035
We snapped his wife's leg.

503
38:37.503 --> 38:39.004
You broke her leg?

504
38:42.800 --> 38:45.052
You damn monsters!

505
38:45.970 --> 38:47.805
What? He speaks Japanese just fine!

506
38:53.060 --> 38:54.812
Oh well, it doesn't matter anymore.

507
38:57.815 --> 38:59.817
-So, what's his name? -Yes.

508
38:59.900 --> 39:01.652
His name is Keum Seok-jung.

509
39:01.735 --> 39:03.571
He's from Kyeam-ri, Suwon.

510
39:12.246 --> 39:13.205
Kyeam-ri?

511
39:13.789 --> 39:17.251
Yes, these two are childhood friends from their hometown in Kyeam-ri.

512
39:26.010 --> 39:27.261
That'll be all for today.

513
39:27.344 --> 39:29.096
We haven't found anything out.

514
39:29.180 --> 39:32.641
He seems fluent in Japanese. We don't need an interpreter anymore.

515
39:34.143 --> 39:36.520
Take these two home in my car.

516
39:36.604 --> 39:37.438
Yes, sir.

517
39:45.404 --> 39:46.822
Let's go, Ms. Keum.

518
39:49.492 --> 39:50.493
Okay.

519
40:03.839 --> 40:04.798
Keum Seo-hee.

520
40:10.763 --> 40:12.056
Is your madam

521
40:14.016 --> 40:15.768
really that good to you?

522
40:16.560 --> 40:18.270
-Shut up! -On your way home,

523
40:19.647 --> 40:22.358
buy a castella cake.

524
40:22.441 --> 40:23.442
Shut up!

525
40:26.570 --> 40:27.488
You need to leave.

526
40:46.382 --> 40:50.719
My daughter is so bright and frugal.

527
40:51.554 --> 40:54.431
Our butler has been staying in bed because of a cold

528
40:54.515 --> 40:56.308
and took three days off.

529
40:56.392 --> 41:00.813
She made sure to remind me to deduct three days from his paycheck.

530
41:02.773 --> 41:05.025
She's that kind of girl.

531
41:11.615 --> 41:13.701
Sir, the chief of police is on the phone.

532
41:13.784 --> 41:14.702
He says it's urgent.

533
41:15.744 --> 41:16.745
Excuse me for a moment.

534
41:16.829 --> 41:17.997
Sure.

535
41:24.003 --> 41:25.087
What is it?

536
41:29.383 --> 41:30.217
What?

537
41:54.825 --> 41:56.410
What did he say at the end?

538
41:59.246 --> 42:00.414
I couldn't hear him.

539
42:00.497 --> 42:01.790
You couldn't hear him?

540
42:01.874 --> 42:04.668
I was going to ask what he said.

541
42:04.752 --> 42:05.836
But I got kicked out.

542
42:09.423 --> 42:10.841
Got it.

543
42:12.509 --> 42:13.510
So…

544
42:15.763 --> 42:19.141
What's going to happen to him now?

545
42:19.725 --> 42:20.726
He'll be put on trial.

546
42:21.602 --> 42:23.812
How many years is he going to get?

547
42:25.606 --> 42:28.984
An attempted assassination alone would get him at least ten years.

548
42:30.152 --> 42:32.821
On top of that, he killed and wounded several police officers.

549
42:32.905 --> 42:35.199
He seriously injured my predecessor, Mr. Suzuki,

550
42:35.282 --> 42:36.575
and tried to kill you too.

551
42:39.203 --> 42:40.996
He could very well be sentenced to death.

552
42:45.793 --> 42:48.087
By the way, isn't Keum Seo-hee your real name?

553
42:52.966 --> 42:53.801
What?

554
42:53.884 --> 42:55.761
Then what's your real name?

555
43:01.183 --> 43:02.059
Lee…

556
43:03.143 --> 43:04.269
Gae-ttong.

557
43:05.479 --> 43:07.690
-What? -That's my real name.

558
43:07.773 --> 43:09.108
Lee Gae-ttong.

559
43:10.150 --> 43:12.736
But now I'm Keum Seo-hee.

560
43:14.822 --> 43:18.075
Please, don't tell anyone at the Government-General about my name.

561
43:18.158 --> 43:18.992
Promise me.

562
43:21.328 --> 43:25.958
And that's how you repay someone who's been so good to you?

563
43:32.339 --> 43:34.258
What did I do?

564
43:35.676 --> 43:39.930
You don't know anything about my relationship with her.

565
43:40.013 --> 43:41.682
I know more than enough.

566
43:42.933 --> 43:44.852
You're having an affair behind someone who's good to you.

567
43:45.686 --> 43:48.897
You confessed your feelings to another man behind your lover's back.

568
43:49.815 --> 43:51.692
Who knows that better than I do?

569
43:55.362 --> 43:57.740
You seem really hung up on what I said.

570
43:57.823 --> 44:00.284
Wouldn't it bother you if you were in my shoes?

571
44:01.243 --> 44:04.163
You say things like that to anyone, so I suppose it means nothing--

572
44:04.246 --> 44:06.039
I don't say that to just anyone.

573
44:07.249 --> 44:10.335
I only said it to you. For the first time in my life.

574
44:14.548 --> 44:15.758
So are you saying…

575
44:17.634 --> 44:20.345
Mr. Yoo is seeing someone who doesn't even like him?

576
44:22.222 --> 44:23.807
Why are you so upset?

577
44:24.850 --> 44:25.768
What?

578
44:25.851 --> 44:29.354
Does it bother you that a woman who's having an affair likes you?

579
44:29.438 --> 44:31.565
Is that why you're so offended?

580
44:33.567 --> 44:35.110
Or maybe,

581
44:35.861 --> 44:39.323
do you hate the thought of me

582
44:39.948 --> 44:40.783
being with Mr. Yoo?

583
44:46.580 --> 44:48.415
Should I stop seeing him?

584
44:48.499 --> 44:50.709
If you tell me to, I will.

585
44:50.793 --> 44:53.295
Will you believe my feelings are genuine then?

586
44:58.050 --> 45:01.094
If I stop seeing Mr. Yoo,

587
45:01.595 --> 45:04.723
I'll be fired from the Government-General, get thrown out on the street,

588
45:04.807 --> 45:06.683
and might never see you again.

589
45:07.684 --> 45:10.103
I'd hate not to see you again,

590
45:10.187 --> 45:13.023
but if that's what you want, I'll do it.

591
45:21.615 --> 45:22.449
Should I

592
45:23.575 --> 45:26.036
end things with Mr. Yoo?

593
45:28.330 --> 45:29.289
If I do,

594
45:31.124 --> 45:33.252
will you accept how I feel about you?

595
45:37.673 --> 45:39.299
Should I break up with him?

596
45:42.010 --> 45:42.845
Yes.

597
45:45.347 --> 45:46.223
Sounds good.

598
45:46.723 --> 45:49.226
While we're at it, let's go see Mr. Yoo now.

599
45:49.309 --> 45:52.020
Break up with him there. Let's go. Lead the way.

600
45:53.146 --> 45:54.064
Come on.

601
45:55.482 --> 45:56.650
What's wrong?

602
45:56.733 --> 45:57.776
Can't you do it?

603
45:59.778 --> 46:01.864
See? You can't break up with him.

604
46:03.407 --> 46:04.533
If you never meant it,

605
46:04.616 --> 46:07.119
how could you talk about breaking up that easily?

606
46:07.911 --> 46:08.745
Well, of course,

607
46:09.872 --> 46:11.999
saying you like someone is a game to you.

608
46:12.082 --> 46:13.834
Watch what you say.

609
46:13.917 --> 46:14.835
Me?

610
46:16.545 --> 46:18.881
Weren't you the one who spoke without thinking?

611
46:19.673 --> 46:23.010
You don't mean a word you say, but you go, "I like you" or "Should I break up?"

612
46:23.760 --> 46:25.762
People like you make me sick.

613
46:26.471 --> 46:28.599
People who throw words around…

614
46:33.020 --> 46:34.479
with no intention of standing by them.

615
46:52.122 --> 46:53.248
Welcome, sir!

616
46:56.251 --> 46:57.419
Is he here?

617
46:57.502 --> 46:58.337
Yes, sir.

618
47:06.845 --> 47:09.222
You must've waited a long time to see me alone.

619
47:10.557 --> 47:11.934
Are you happy now?

620
47:12.809 --> 47:13.644
Keum Seok-jung.

621
47:15.729 --> 47:17.105
Has it been 13 years?

622
47:20.776 --> 47:22.486
Seeing you again,

623
47:23.445 --> 47:24.613
I think I remember you.

624
47:26.365 --> 47:29.910
Ishikawa Nobuyuki.

625
47:32.579 --> 47:33.997
A mass murderer.

626
47:36.667 --> 47:39.211
You killed my family, my friends,

627
47:40.462 --> 47:43.215
and everyone in my village, then burned them all.

628
47:45.550 --> 47:46.969
You're a mass murderer.

629
47:51.473 --> 47:52.724
Mass murder?

630
47:52.808 --> 47:55.394
I was simply carrying out my official duty.

631
47:55.477 --> 47:56.812
I was putting down a riot.

632
47:57.854 --> 47:59.064
A riot?

633
48:01.149 --> 48:03.944
All we did was peacefully cry out for our independence.

634
48:04.027 --> 48:07.239
We demanded our stolen nation back.

635
48:07.322 --> 48:08.740
And what did you do?

636
48:10.367 --> 48:12.911
You locked us up.

637
48:18.000 --> 48:19.793
You shot us and burned us alive.

638
48:40.313 --> 48:42.649
In retaliation for the independence movement.

639
48:43.275 --> 48:44.443
Retaliation?

640
48:46.153 --> 48:46.987
No.

641
48:48.947 --> 48:50.240
Japan doesn't have time

642
48:50.907 --> 48:54.119
to bother with retaliating against uncivilized Joseon people.

643
48:55.662 --> 48:57.706
I was cleared of all charges in court.

644
48:59.124 --> 49:01.043
I guess you never saw the verdict.

645
49:01.710 --> 49:06.089
Are you denying everything you ordered with your own mouth?

646
49:12.262 --> 49:14.723
Aren't you afraid of being haunted

647
49:16.141 --> 49:17.642
by those who died that day?

648
49:24.900 --> 49:28.612
Imagine how much your wife resented you.

649
49:31.740 --> 49:34.493
Did it ever cross your mind that it was all your fault?

650
49:36.036 --> 49:39.414
Have you never thought about how all those people who died that day

651
49:40.999 --> 49:42.167
must resent you?

652
49:45.837 --> 49:50.217
If you hadn't lured those naive people into your little independence protest,

653
49:52.052 --> 49:53.595
they'd all still be alive.

654
49:55.430 --> 49:58.517
And you'd still be with your family,

655
49:59.476 --> 50:02.229
enjoying a happy life together.

656
50:05.816 --> 50:06.942
Happy?

657
50:09.402 --> 50:11.029
Did you just say "happy"?

658
50:13.240 --> 50:15.242
In a country that's been stolen from us?

659
50:15.909 --> 50:16.827
Happy?

660
50:43.770 --> 50:46.523
Those were gunshots, right?

661
50:58.577 --> 51:00.704
They must've been quite the loving couple,

662
51:01.746 --> 51:03.874
dying side by side at the same time.

663
51:07.127 --> 51:09.004
You know, your friend from Kyeam-ri.

664
51:10.380 --> 51:11.339
What was his name?

665
51:11.923 --> 51:12.757
Na…

666
51:12.841 --> 51:15.135
Na whatever-his-name-was?

667
51:17.220 --> 51:19.514
Ishikawa!

668
51:24.811 --> 51:26.897
Aren't you afraid of karma?

669
51:28.857 --> 51:31.026
Mark my words!

670
51:33.069 --> 51:36.156
You will pay dearly for what you've done.

671
51:36.239 --> 51:37.657
Don't worry.

672
51:39.743 --> 51:42.162
I'm not going to kill you.

673
51:43.622 --> 51:44.664
Your cause of death…

674
51:47.542 --> 51:48.501
will be an illness.

675
51:52.088 --> 51:53.048
Fukuda!

676
52:07.520 --> 52:08.355
Ms. Keum.

677
52:09.356 --> 52:10.523
Listen to me carefully.

678
52:10.607 --> 52:12.859
Whatever you're assuming, you've got it wrong.

679
52:13.652 --> 52:16.071
He's going to face trial, which will take months.

680
52:16.154 --> 52:17.030
So…

681
52:17.906 --> 52:18.740
Ms. Keum!

682
52:20.367 --> 52:21.284
Keum Seo-hee!

683
53:30.186 --> 53:31.479
Interpreter Trainee Keum.

684
53:39.779 --> 53:41.698
Great work interpreting the interrogation today.

685
53:42.782 --> 53:44.117
But I have some bad news.

686
53:44.909 --> 53:47.120
The suspect just died.

687
53:48.913 --> 53:51.166
It looks like his gunshot wound led to sepsis.

688
53:58.131 --> 53:59.215
I see.

689
54:02.135 --> 54:03.470
That's a shame.

690
54:05.805 --> 54:07.974
What a weak man he was.

691
54:11.644 --> 54:12.854
If you'll excuse me.

692
54:59.901 --> 55:03.822
The chief of police told me to drive you both home.

693
55:06.574 --> 55:07.534
Get in.

694
55:08.701 --> 55:09.828
They'll take you home.

695
55:11.371 --> 55:12.205
I'm okay.

696
55:13.790 --> 55:15.208
I'll go on my own.

697
55:49.993 --> 55:51.369
You call this okay?

698
55:54.831 --> 55:55.832
Look at you.

699
55:56.332 --> 55:57.917
Your hands are shaking.

700
56:08.136 --> 56:10.180
We've got the Na Byeong-sun couple down as suicides,

701
56:10.263 --> 56:13.558
and Keum Seok-jung as dying of acute sepsis.

702
56:14.726 --> 56:15.560
Very well.

703
56:16.561 --> 56:18.021
Sir, there's one thing.

704
56:19.647 --> 56:22.567
Keum Seo-hee saw Keum Seok-jung's body.

705
56:23.151 --> 56:24.360
Will that be all right?

706
56:24.861 --> 56:26.613
She saw the dead body?

707
56:26.696 --> 56:27.822
Yes, sir.

708
56:27.906 --> 56:30.992
She came to the interrogation room with Hideo out of the blue.

709
56:32.827 --> 56:33.661
With Hideo?

710
56:33.745 --> 56:34.829
Yes, sir.

711
56:35.747 --> 56:37.665
I told her he died of septic shock.

712
56:42.337 --> 56:43.588
But since she saw it,

713
56:44.422 --> 56:46.341
if Yoo Philip hears about it,

714
56:46.424 --> 56:49.177
it could turn into a big problem like the Kyeam-ri incident.

715
56:50.929 --> 56:53.973
Back then, a foreign reporter got word out to the foreign press,

716
56:54.599 --> 56:56.684
and that's how we ended up in court.

717
57:01.397 --> 57:03.858
Things are already complicated with Manchuria,

718
57:03.942 --> 57:06.069
and Westerners won't stop talking.

719
57:06.569 --> 57:07.529
I'm afraid

720
57:08.321 --> 57:10.782
they'll start digging up Kyeam-ri all over again--

721
57:10.865 --> 57:11.699
Fukuda.

722
57:11.783 --> 57:12.909
Yes, sir.

723
57:14.160 --> 57:16.746
Keum Seok-jung died of an illness during interrogation.

724
57:17.455 --> 57:19.707
What does that have to do with Yoo Philip?

725
57:22.126 --> 57:23.002
My mistake, sir.

726
57:23.920 --> 57:26.089
I got confused for a moment.

727
57:29.592 --> 57:30.843
On another note,

728
57:32.262 --> 57:34.889
did you know Keum is a rare family name?

729
57:36.140 --> 57:36.975
Pardon?

730
57:39.352 --> 57:40.979
Call the Suwon Police Station.

731
57:41.479 --> 57:44.482
Have them find Keum Seok-jung's personal records and send them over.

732
57:45.024 --> 57:46.234
There should be a record

733
57:47.318 --> 57:48.778
from 13 years ago.

734
57:50.363 --> 57:51.197
Yes, sir.

735
58:00.957 --> 58:02.375
Keum Seok-jung.

736
58:03.960 --> 58:05.003
Keum Seo-hee.

737
58:34.157 --> 58:34.991
What?

738
58:37.535 --> 58:38.578
You're lonely?

739
58:39.746 --> 58:43.124
Koharu, how can I say that here?

740
58:44.083 --> 58:46.210
I told you I'm at work.

741
58:48.463 --> 58:49.297
What?

742
58:50.923 --> 58:52.300
I said I can't.

743
58:53.259 --> 58:55.511
I really can't.

744
58:57.430 --> 58:59.140
Why won't you stop?

745
59:08.399 --> 59:09.859
You're so silly.

746
59:18.868 --> 59:20.203
We're here.

747
59:37.512 --> 59:38.888
Thank you…

748
59:40.765 --> 59:42.016
for bringing me home.

749
01:00:28.104 --> 01:00:30.606
How am I supposed to tell her?

750
01:01:23.701 --> 01:01:24.786
Ms. Keum.

751
01:01:31.793 --> 01:01:33.002
Are you okay?

752
01:01:39.300 --> 01:01:40.134
Yes.

753
01:01:42.637 --> 01:01:43.763
I'm fi…

754
01:01:55.900 --> 01:01:56.734
No.

755
01:01:57.902 --> 01:01:59.403
I'm not.

756
01:03:29.201 --> 01:03:33.039
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

757
01:03:33.998 --> 01:03:36.292
I don't belong anywhere anyway.

758
01:03:36.375 --> 01:03:37.251
Why?

759
01:03:37.835 --> 01:03:40.338
Have you had a change of heart since coming to Joseon?

760
01:03:40.421 --> 01:03:43.257
Ms. Keum, you're a good person.

761
01:03:44.258 --> 01:03:47.511
Look into Keum Seo-hee's record. Her past, all of it. Leave nothing out.

762
01:03:47.595 --> 01:03:49.805
What happened in the past?

763
01:03:49.889 --> 01:03:52.558
He should have been given a proper trial.

764
01:03:52.642 --> 01:03:53.726
I have no regrets.

765
01:03:53.809 --> 01:03:55.519
Could it be Kyeam-ri?

766
01:03:55.603 --> 01:03:56.979
-A family photo? -Ms. Keum?

767
01:03:57.063 --> 01:03:58.230
What is that

768
01:03:59.357 --> 01:04:00.274
in your hand?

769
01:04:07.573 --> 01:04:09.575
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
